-- title:
--   Level-two node ring as a localisation of an integral closure
-- statement:
--   Let $q\ge 5$ be a prime, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, let $k$ be a field of characteristic $q$ and $\mathrm{red}\colon A\to k$ a ring homomorphism. Let $a\in k$ lie in `ssJSet q k`, i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $k$ with $j$-invariant $a$ has no nonzero point killed by $q$, and assume $a^{q^2}=a$ and $a\in\{0,1728\}$. Let $K$ be a finite extension of $\mathbb Q$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, write $A_0:=$ `coeffSubring A K` $=A\cap K$ and let $\overline{\mathrm{red}}\colon A_0\to k$ be the restriction of $\mathrm{red}$. Let $l\in k$ satisfy $a\,(16l)^2(16l-1)^2=256\bigl((16l)^2-16l+1\bigr)^3$ and admit a lift $y\in A_0$ with $\overline{\mathrm{red}}(y)=l$. Write $R:=$ `modularLocalizedAtPoint (1*q) A₀ red l`-style level-one node ring, namely the subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}(\!(\mathsf q)\!)$ of Laurent series $f$ for which there are $r,s\in A_0[X_0,X_1]$ with $\overline{\mathrm{red}}$-evaluation $s(a,a^q)\ne 0$ and $f\cdot s(j,j_q)=r(j,j_q)$, where $j,j_q$ are the $q$-expansion series `jqModC`, `jqNModC` at level $1\cdot q$; and let $S:=$ `lambdaLocalizedAtPoint q A₀ (redRestrict red K) l (l^q)` be the analogous ring built from the Legendre series `lambdaModC`, `lambdaNModC` at level $q$ and the point $(l,l^q)$, assumed to be a local ring. Finally let $B$ be a subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}(\!(\mathsf q)\!)$ whose elements are exactly the $z$ lying in `lambdaFieldOver q K` (the subfield generated by the constant series from $K$ together with `lambdaModC` and `lambdaNModC` at level $q$) which are integral over the image of $R$ under the $q$-expansion operator $\varphi:=$ `qExpand (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) 2`. Then: (i) $\varphi(z)\in B$ for every $z\in R$; (ii) $p(\lambda,\lambda_q)\in B$ for every $p\in A_0[X_0,X_1]$, i.e. `lambdaEval q A₀ p` $\in B$; and (iii) $B\le S$, and for the inclusion $B\hookrightarrow S$ and the prime $\mathfrak P$ obtained by contracting the maximal ideal of $S$ to $B$: $\mathfrak P$ is maximal, $S$ is the localisation of $B$ at $\mathfrak P$, and `lambdaEval q A₀ p` lies in $\mathfrak P$ whenever $p\in A_0[X_0,X_1]$ satisfies $p(l,l^q)=0$ after $\overline{\mathrm{red}}$-evaluation.
--
--   This identifies the level-two (Legendre) node ring at a supersingular node of the plane model of $X_0(q)$, for $j$-invariant $0$ or $1728$, with the localisation at the node of the integral closure of the image of the level-one node ring in the level-two function field. It is used in the comparison of the maximal ideal of the level-two node ring with contractions from that integral closure, and in the construction of a subring of an adic completion equivariant for a stabiliser, in the $j\in\{0,1728\}$ case.
